WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.600
Senpai, I'll ask her.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.220
I'll ask Asuka-senpai why you can't come back.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.070
She's gorgeous.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.940
Good job, Taki-sensei.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.560
Asuka-senpai, there's something 
I want to talk to you about.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.750
<b>Clinic Room 1</b>

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.750
Okay, let's start with breathing.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.880
Breathe in deep, and think about 
the distance as you exhale.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:59.550
<i>Our morning meetings involve 
all of us breathing together</i>

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.360
<i>and doing vocal exercises.</i>

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.350
<i>Then we move on to sectional practice.</i>

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.100
<i>And in the afternoon, it's non-stop rehearsal.</i>

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.330
All right, let's move on to ten in a row.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.520
Yes!

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.870
<i>By "ten in a row," he means playing the 
required piece and free-choice piece</i>

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.200
<i>ten times in a row, back-to-back.</i>

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.490
<i>Together, the two are about 12 minutes.</i>

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:34.460
<i>With a 2-minute break each time, 
it takes at least 160 minutes.</i>

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.300
<i>By the end, everyone ends up like this.</i>

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.180
All right, let's take twenty.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.190
Twenty minutes, huh?

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.790
I think I'll go play for a bit!

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.310
Holy crap...

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.820
Do you have some time later?

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:58.240
What is it? Do you want to 
talk about relationships?

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.240
Could you not do that? This is serious.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:05.120
I wish we could keep the serious 
talk to our performances...

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:07.730
Okay, sure.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.500
When did you want to?

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.740
After dinner, then.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.760
<i>The time was approaching.</i>

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.760
<i>Episode 3 
Troubled Nocturnes</i>

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:34.600
That's the idea, but this piece has 
a lot of simple B-flat measures.

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.570
Let's focus on getting those together.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:38.950
Yes!

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:42.240
Also, the snare is dragging a little.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.110
Keep it moving forward!

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:44.780
Yes.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.710
And... Timpani!

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:47.730
Yes.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.590
That part was a beat early, right?

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.250
Yes.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.290
This isn't the time for that...

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.710
I could fine you for it.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:57.810
Yes!

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.810
All right, once more, from the top.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:04.760
Tuba, you're holding your G-flat for too long.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.010
Your fingers are fast enough, but your 
chops aren't keeping up.

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:12.000
Is that the best you can do in tempo?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.360
All right, that's enough.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:26.970
For this part, please keep that 
last performance in mind.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.330
Euphoniums...

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.280
Yes.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:32.000
Please play that part together

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.540
for the Kansai Competition.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.750
Yes.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.680
Oumae-san?

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:39.630
Yes?

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.840
Your answer?

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.050
Yes.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:55.020
Say, Taki-kun, are you satisfied 
with the oboe solo?

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:02.460
I mean, you sound great, 
and you're always in tune.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:06.740
But honestly, in a word, it's boring.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.460
It's like a robot's playing.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:11.700
A robot?

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.290
A machine could read the notes off 
the page just as well as you.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.190
Yoroizuka-san?

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.280
Yes?

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:21.170
What are you going for with this solo?

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.090
What do you feel when you're playing?

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.840
A crescent moon.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:31.100
Make it sound more 
like a crescent moon, then!

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:33.270
I'll do better.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:36.870
I think saying you'll "do better" is bad enough.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.730
Can't you be more expressive?

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:40.190
I'm sorry...

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.090
You don't have to apologize.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:45.240
I think collected girls are charming.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.880
But you can't be collected for this solo!

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:53.870
You have to be, like, "Hear me, 
I'm the best in the world!"

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.290
You know, like the trumpet girl's solo.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:01.270
Honestly, your playing gets better and better.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:04.460
You're up there with those 
from the best schools.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.120
But you lack expression.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:10.000
That's the big difference 
between you and them.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.090
What kind of music is Kitauji trying to make?

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.680
In this camp, that's what 
I want you to work on.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:16.990
Yes.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:20.200
Coming from you, Hashimoto-sensei, 
that was surprisingly good.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.770
Did you have to say, "Coming from you"?

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.570
I'm a walking book of famous quotes.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:30.410
All right, let's do that part once more.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:38.160
I'm so hungry...

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.000
You'll be late for bath time.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.000
No way, it's that time already?

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.750
<b>Bath Schedule</b>

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.630
Man, we only have ten minutes.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:50.930
Don't let it get to you.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:51.640
But...

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.800
It's all right.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:58.630
He just wants you to aim higher 
because you're so good.

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.020
Yoroizuka-senpai...

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.410
Kumiko,

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:07.440
I think I'm going to ask Taki-sensei 
during the fireworks...

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.160
If he's in a relationship with Niiyama-sensei.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:13.870
Yeah?

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.200
<b>Café and Restaurant 
Nature Farm</b>

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:20.640
I love mapo tofu, too!

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.290
Time to eat!

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:27.800
<i>Reina... It must really be weighing on her.</i>

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.040
Oumae-chan!

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.180
Should I just stay behind?

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.290
Sure...

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.640
Sorry.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.650
No problem.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:46.670
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:55.410
Um... Why won't you allow
Nozomi-senpai to return?

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:00.830
Why do <i>you </i>want to know, Oumae-chan?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.040
Can she not?

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.500
It isn't that she can't, but...

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.590
Oh, are you actually a gossip?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.350
That isn't it!

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:13.380
I promised Nozomi-senpai that 
I'd ask you for the truth...

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.750
You said that?

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:19.300
You shouldn't make promises like that.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:20.720
Sh-Should I not have?

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:24.310
I mean it's fine, but it'll haunt you later.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.280
Why would it?

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:30.650
Why do you think it is that I won't 
accept her coming back?

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:33.030
I'm the one asking.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.740
Aw, come on.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:38.530
I thought, maybe, because 
Nozomi-senpai is so good,

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:42.330
it could cause confusion in 
the club if she came back.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.460
I see!

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.750
Nice try, but you're totally wrong.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.900
Then, what is it?

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.300
If I tell you, you'll be miserable.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.260
Are you okay with that?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:52.970
Huh?

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:55.680
I'll tell you if you're okay with that.

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:58.640
Please tell me.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.730
You're so smart. And yet you're such a fool.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:04.940
I warned you.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:09.110
You know the oboe, Mizore Yoroizuka-chan?

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.150
Yes.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:13.410
She can't stand Nozomi-chan.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:16.490
Just seeing her face sickens her.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:18.710
She has some trauma.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:25.040
But Nozomi-chan has no idea that 
that's how she feels about her.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:28.830
She thinks they're still good 
friends that go way back.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:34.280
I can't say, "Mizore-chan can't play 
the oboe with you around,

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:37.550
so don't come back," can I?

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.390
Even I'm not that much of a monster.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:45.680
We only have one oboe in our band.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:50.650
If Mizore-chan went down now, Kansai would 
be the least of our worries.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:56.110
If we have to pick between the two, 
isn't our choice pretty obvious?

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.720
That's the truth.

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:01.580
What will you choose?

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:06.000
Will you tell Nozomi-chan 
what I just explained?

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:10.780
See, I told you...

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:13.570
You're better off pretending you 
didn't hear anything, I guess.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:17.970
Tell her, "Asuka-senpai wouldn't say anything."

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.070
Fireworks! Fireworks!

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:29.310
Look, they're so pretty!

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:29.680
Look out!

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.190
Don't swing them around!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:34.190
But they're so pretty...

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:40.030
Want to try?

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:41.740
Yeah.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:46.450
It's been a while since I've 
done anything like this.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.150
Me, too.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:57.970
You should throw it out.

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:00.330
Your sparkler.

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:04.940
I'm not emotionally prepared yet.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:08.540
You'd better hurry. Niiyama-sensei is 
going to come back.

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.230
I think it's now or never.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:13.820
But if he told me they're dating—

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:18.430
I'll go.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:22.030
Off you go.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.930
Does that girl have a crush on Taki-kun?

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.880
Taki-kun's such a player.

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.590
You were listening?

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:34.000
Nah.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.940
I picked it up from her gaze and stuff.

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:38.150
I'm technically a grown-up, after all.

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:39.210
I see.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:44.180
I'm relieved to see Taki-kun smiling, though.

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:49.770
Ever since he lost his wife, 
Taki-kun's been down.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.560
Yeah... Wait!

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:53.940
Crap.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.420
Taki-sensei was married?

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:59.200
Sensei!

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.120
He was.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.860
But she passed away five years ago.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:11.960
Next up, the trombones will be 
holding an imitation contest!

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.670
What is this?

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:21.700
Ever since his wife passed away, 
Taki-kun's been like a husk.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:25.090
He distanced himself from music, too.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:28.010
All of us were worried.

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:35.940
So I was really happy when I heard 
he'd become the adviser at Kitauji.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:41.150
I nearly cried when he asked me 
to help out with teaching.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:00.210
Taki-sensei isn't dating her.

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:02.630
No?

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:05.470
Apparently, Niiyama-sensei is married.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:07.930
That's good.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.260
Yeah.

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:17.080
<i>I couldn't bring myself to tell Reina 
about Taki-sensei's past.</i>

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:50.140
I like Taki-sensei.

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:53.780
Maybe I should tell her...

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:57.350
I told you that it's nothing.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:58.740
You're lying.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:00.190
Tell me the truth.

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:03.400
Why can't Nozomi rejoin the club?

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:06.610
I never said she couldn't.

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:08.930
There's a reason, isn't there?

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:10.120
What is it?

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.600
Nothing...

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:15.530
I just think it might cause chaos in 
the band if she came back now.

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:18.540
And I told you that Nozomi would only help.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.170
Regardless, no!

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:24.090
Then that isn't the only reason, is it?

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:25.720
Something's going on.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.510
What is it?

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:34.520
I told you not to get involved. 
It'll just cause a huge mess!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.030
That's all!

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:37.980
Hey.

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:53.910
What do you want?

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:54.890
Huh?

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:56.230
To drink.

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:58.600
Orange juice, then.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:14:59.710
Okay.

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:03.920
So, do you hate me?

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.280
I don't hate you. I just don't like you...

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:10.840
Do you still hold a grudge about what 
happened at the Kyoto Competition?

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:16.470
Just so you know, I'm definitely 
not in the wrong about it!

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:21.090
I still think Kaori-senpai should play the solo.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:22.650
Sure...

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:25.200
Senpai's seriously an angel.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:28.540
She's cute and kind, and I just can't...

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:31.310
What's up with that reaction?

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:33.240
You're supposed to respond with a witticism.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.780
Oh, you were kidding?

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.250
I mean...

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:41.920
Last year, we second-years 
had a lot going on.

00:15:42.530 --> 00:15:46.380
I thought pretty hard about
quitting concert band, too.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:51.090
That's when Kaori-senpai cheered me on.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:55.750
I heard a bit about it from Natsuki-senpai.

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:57.100
About last year.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:00.230
So it's been bugging you, too?

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.310
I guess.

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:02.490
Well?

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:07.050
How much of what we were 
saying earlier did you hear?

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:11.740
Asuka-senpai also knows, huh?

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.740
Of course she does.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:17.760
Just so we're clear,
you'd better not tell Natsuki.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.750
Huh? Why not?

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:23.210
Natsuki-senpai might help us out.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:26.490
Why would I want her help? 
I don't need that noise.

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:28.380
Noise?

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:32.610
Besides, Natsuki is genuinely 
trying to get Nozomi back

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:34.850
into the club for her sake.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.430
Judging by her personality,

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:42.480
Natsuki wouldn't know what to 
do if she heard about Mizore.

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.150
Do you hate competitions, Senpai?

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:54.890
Where did that come from?

00:16:54.890 --> 00:17:00.580
Sorry, earlier you mentioned 
Kaori-senpai's solo, so...

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:04.280
What's the deal with competitions, huh?

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:09.130
Well, there definitely is a lot 
about them that's frustrating.

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:13.180
I'm not satisfied with how my last competition

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:15.550
in middle school turned out, either.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.800
<b>Second Place, Minami Public Middle School</b>

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:19.810
But that's only because it turned out badly.

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:24.020
If it had turned out well, I probably 
would have accepted it.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:26.540
Just like us right now.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.730
That makes sense.

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:31.110
We aren't just messing around.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:34.240
We've all sacrificed our summer 
breaks to practice.

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:40.200
Yet competitions assign superiority: 
gold, silver, bronze.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:44.020
Sometimes, they don't even 
hesitate to write things like

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:47.350
"You were doomed the moment you chose 
this piece" on the evaluation forms,

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:49.420
no matter how well you performed.

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:54.630
You're judged as not having put in the 
effort, as having been inferior.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:56.560
How does that even follow?

00:17:57.190 --> 00:18:01.850
Then, you think competitions shouldn't exist?

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:05.020
Sure, I've thought that, sometimes.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:07.240
But if you asked me

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:10.200
if we should play casually, 
just for the heck of it,

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:14.350
like we did last year... 
That wasn't right, either.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:19.450
I didn't like that the lazy third-years 
were getting into the competition,

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:23.740
even as the first-years were 
aiming high and working hard.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:28.960
I mean, a lot's happened since we 
became meritocratic this year.

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:34.520
I think that if we're serious about
the Nationals, the better players should play.

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.640
Senpai, isn't that—

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:41.010
Ultimately, if we're going to 
enter the competitions,

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:44.420
we should go for gold, shouldn't we?

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.320
Crap, look at the time.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:49.560
I'm going back to my room.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.010
Okay.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.570
I totally lost out on sleep.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.120
Where were you?

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:06.190
You were awake...

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:09.250
Didn't you sneak out yesterday, too?

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.000
Yeah, stuff.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.310
Tsukamoto?

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:14.960
Why would you go there?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.960
He has nothing to do with it.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:20.220
<b>Please cover futons with sheets!! 
How to fold futons</b>

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:19.460
Hey, Reina...

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:22.720
What do you think of competitions?

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.110
Why?

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:27.190
I've just been thinking about them.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:33.820
A lot of people say you can't really judge music

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:37.740
using only gold, silver, or bronze.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:41.540
I think only winners get to say that.

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:45.800
When bad players say it, I think it's 
nothing more than sour grapes.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:52.250
So, in the end, the only thing 
to do is to get good.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:57.020
Besides, you don't really get 
many opportunities to have

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:58.510
a lot of people listen to you.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.550
I like them.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:07.260
I want to be positive about them.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:11.770
Yeah?

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:38.910
I got no sleep at all.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:46.890
Pretty.

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:54.230
Euphonium?

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:19.180
Asuka-senpai...

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:44.060
<i>It was a strange piece, somehow. 
A warm, lonely piece.</i>

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:49.120
<i>It seemed to convey a myriad of emotions.</i>

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:08.280
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:09.930
<b>To Be Continued</b>
